# Comment Bank

A human-readable reference for feedback comments, organised for quick lookup while marking.

---

## 📝 Framework
{.category #framework}

Opening/closing comments, overall structure.

### Openings

> Thank you for your submission. I've read through your work and have the following feedback.
{#fw-001}

> Hi {student-name}, thank you for submitting {tma}. {overall-impression}
{#fw-002 .template}

### Closings

> Overall, this is a solid piece of work. Keep up the good effort.
{#fw-003}

> Please review the specific feedback below and feel free to ask questions on the forum if anything is unclear.
{#fw-004}

> Best regards,
> {tutor-name}
> {module} Tutor
{#fw-005 .template}

---

## 📌 Margin
{.category #margin}

Short annotations for document margins. Quick, punchy.

### Positive

| Shortcut | Text |
|----------|------|
| `+good` | Good point |
| `+well` | Well explained |
| `+example` | Excellent example |

### Concerns

| Shortcut | Text |
|----------|------|
| `?unclear` | Unclear - please expand |
| `?source` | Source needed |
| `?check` | Check this |
| `?meaning` | What do you mean here? |

### Structure

| Shortcut | Text |
|----------|------|
| `~link` | Link to previous point |

---

## ✏️ In-Text
{.category #inline}

Comments inserted within the student's answer. Use `[square brackets]` to show they're insertions.

### Referencing

- **Harvard format**: Please use Harvard referencing format: (Author, Year).
  {#in-001}

- **Missing reference**: [Reference needed to support this claim]
  {#in-002}

### Clarity

- **Rephrase**: [Consider rephrasing for clarity]
  {#in-003}

- **Define term**: [Technical term - define on first use]
  {#in-004}

### Quality

- **Grammar**: [Check grammar/spelling here]
  {#in-005}

- **Logic gap**: [The connection here isn't clear - how does this follow?]
  {#in-006}

- **Strengthen**: [Good point - strengthen with specific evidence]
  {#in-007}

---

## 📊 Summary
{.category #summary}

Longer comments for overall feedback sections.

### Positive Feedback

> You demonstrate a clear understanding of the key concepts. Your explanations are accurate and well-structured.
{#sm-001 .positive}

### Development Areas

> While you've covered the basics well, try to go deeper in your analysis. Ask yourself 'why' and 'how' to develop your points further.
{#sm-002 .development}

> The structure of your answer could be improved. Consider using headings to organise your response around the question's sub-parts.
{#sm-003 .structure}

> Your referencing needs attention throughout. Remember: every claim from an external source needs a citation, and all citations need a full reference in your bibliography.
{#sm-004 .referencing}

### Higher-Level Skills

> You've described the topic well, but at this level we're looking for critical evaluation. Consider: What are the limitations? What alternatives exist? What evidence supports or contradicts this view?
{#sm-005 .critical}

> Good theoretical understanding. To strengthen your work, try to include practical examples that show how these concepts apply in real situations.
{#sm-006 .practical}

### Encouragement

> This submission shows improvement from your previous work. You've clearly taken the earlier feedback on board. Keep building on this progress.
{#sm-007 .progress}

